<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- BIO-INT-001 owns api/features/bio-int-001/** only. No ProjectReference to
         Biolog.Api.csproj (one-way dependency, scripts/check-module-project-references.sh)
         and none to bio-idn-006 either - BIO-IDN-006's RoleAssignmentService/PermissionService
         are internal with InternalsVisibleTo granted only to Biolog.Api and its own test
         assembly, and this project cannot reference a sibling feature project any more than
         it can reference the host. Role names this project's ClaimMappingRule may target are
         therefore this project's OWN closed, documented copy of BIO-IDN-006's RoleType wire
         strings (see Domain/KnownRoles.cs) - a duplicated value set, not a live reference,
         the same "duplicate the minimal shape" boundary pattern BIO-DEV-003's
         DeviceDescriptor and BIO-RPT-001's DomainEventEnvelope already established.

         Tenant resolution: every method takes a plain string tenantId, same as
         BIO-RPT-001 - api/Biolog.Api/Modules/BioInt001Module.cs resolves the real
         ITenantContextAccessor and passes the string down.

         No JWT/session ADR exists anywhere in this codebase (confirmed by search before
         designing - docs/features/bio-crd-007/README.md already states this explicitly for
         its own signed-package feature). Session tokens here are a hand-rolled HMAC-signed
         opaque string (Domain/SessionToken.cs), the same shape as BIO-IDN-006's own
         ActorProvenanceGate HMAC precedent - not a JWT library dependency, so no new
         vulnerability-scan surface is introduced for a foundation story. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.Authentication.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
